SET
  @Description_a0c1bfa2b83b = N'Returns the newest MJ: ML Training Runs row of one training pipeline whose Status is Running and that started after the given instant, or no row. Predictive Studio auto-train reads it under the pipeline lock to claim the pipeline for one training at a time (single-flight, D4-12): a run in flight means another training owns the pipeline.'
SET
  @SQL_a0c1bfa2b83b = N'-- Predictive Studio auto-train: the training run of one pipeline that is in flight now, if any.
--
-- TrainingClaims.ClaimPipeline runs this through RunQuery inside its transaction, after it holds the
-- pipeline lock (Predictive Studio: Lock Pipeline For Publish), so every claim of one pipeline reads
-- it in turn and sees the run row the previous claim committed (D4-12: the claim is the run row). A
-- Running run that started at or before StartedAfter (the caller passes now minus the stale threshold,
-- 6 h by default) is stale and does not block a new claim. Returns the newest in-flight run, or no
-- row. SQL Server only (D-057).
SELECT TOP 1 ID, StartedAt
FROM [${flyway:defaultSchema}].MLTrainingRun
WHERE PipelineID = {{ PipelineID | sqlString }}
  AND Status = ''Running''
  AND StartedAt > {{ StartedAfter | sqlString }}
ORDER BY StartedAt DESC
'
SET
  @TechnicalDescription_a0c1bfa2b83b = N'SELECT TOP 1 ID, StartedAt FROM MLTrainingRun WHERE PipelineID = PipelineID AND Status = ''Running'' AND StartedAt > StartedAfter ORDER BY StartedAt DESC. Runs inside the caller''s transaction after Predictive Studio: Lock Pipeline For Publish has locked the pipeline, so two claims of one pipeline read it in turn and the second sees the run row the first committed (TrainingClaims.ClaimPipeline). StartedAfter is an ISO 8601 UTC instant (now minus the stale threshold, 6 h by default): an older Running row is a stale claim and does not block. Single statement. SQL Server only (D-057).'
