  )
SET
  @UserQuestion_5ca2484da193 = N'Hold this scoring binding for my scoring batch and tell me its current status, so a withdrawal cannot clear the binding''s predictions while my batch is still writing them.'
SET
  @Description_5ca2484da193 = N'Takes a shared lock on one MJ: ML Model Scoring Bindings row for the rest of the caller''s transaction and returns its Status. Predictive Studio''s scoring service runs it first in every writing batch and stops the run when the binding is Withdrawn; a withdrawal waits for the batches in flight.'
SET
  @SQL_5ca2484da193 = N'-- Predictive Studio scoring: lock one scoring binding row for a scoring batch and read its current Status.
--
-- ScoringService runs this through RunQuery as the first statement of each writing batch''s transaction and
-- stops the run when the returned Status is Withdrawn. HOLDLOCK holds a shared lock on the binding row until
-- the batch commits or rolls back, and it is a locking read even under READ_COMMITTED_SNAPSHOT, so:
--   * a withdrawal committed before the batch is always seen (never an older row version);
--   * ScoringBindings.Withdraw, whose first write updates this row''s Status, waits for every batch in flight
--     to commit and then clears what those batches wrote.
-- Shared locks are compatible, so concurrent runs of one binding do not wait for each other here.
-- Returns one row when the binding exists, none otherwise. SQL Server only (D-057).
SELECT Status
FROM [${flyway:defaultSchema}].MLModelScoringBinding WITH (HOLDLOCK)
WHERE ID = {{ BindingID | sqlString }}
'
SET
  @TechnicalDescription_5ca2484da193 = N'SELECT Status FROM MLModelScoringBinding WITH (HOLDLOCK) WHERE ID = BindingID. Must run inside the caller''s transaction on the caller''s provider: the shared (and key-range) lock is held until commit or rollback, and HOLDLOCK makes it a locking read under READ_COMMITTED_SNAPSHOT too. ScoringBindings.Withdraw updates the row''s Status first in its own transaction, so it waits for every batch holding the lock and its clearing of the binding''s values and copies sees what they wrote (review R5, D4-289). Shared locks are compatible: concurrent runs of one binding do not serialise. Returns one row when the binding exists, none otherwise. Single statement. SQL Server only (D-057).'
